[h1]World Map Zoom 1.0[/h1]
See the native world map at 2x or 4x. Drag to move around and hover over places
to inspect them. Text and buttons keep their normal size.

[b]Requires DFHack and a separate manual installation. Subscribing alone does not enable zoom.[/b]

[h2]Get the working mod[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/Huitzilopochtli-98/df-world-map-zoom/releases/tag/v1.0.0]Download the Windows 1.0.0 release[/url]
Choose WorldMapZoom-1.0.0-windows-x64.zip, close the game, and extract the ZIP.
Open the WorldMapZoom folder, type powershell into File Explorer's address bar,
and press Enter. Run:
[code]powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\Install.ps1[/code]

Restart the game and open the fortress world map or embark world map.
Press Ctrl+Shift+D, enter gui/worldmap-zoom, and press Enter.

[h2]Supported versions[/h2]
Windows 64-bit, Steam Dwarf Fortress 53.16, DFHack 53.16-r3.
The installer checks the exact supported builds. Other builds need a compatible release.

[h2]What subscribing provides[/h2]
This item adds the DFHack help command worldmap-zoom-setup with the installation
instructions and download link. It does not contain or automatically install the
native zoom DLL. You do not need to select this companion when creating a world.

[h2]Controls after installing the Windows package[/h2]
Mouse wheel or +/- buttons: zoom. Left/middle drag or arrows/WASD: move.
Z: cycle 1x, 2x, 4x. R: reset. I: toggle native selection. Esc/right-click: close.

[h2]Updating and removal[/h2]
Workshop updates apply to this help companion. Updating the native zoom feature
requires running the installer from the new Windows release with the game closed.
Unsubscribing does not remove the manually installed plugin. Use Install.ps1
-Uninstall from the extracted Windows package to remove that plugin.

